! STEOM-DLPNO-CCSD def2-SVPD RIJCOSX TightSCF TightPNO AutoAux
# 44-atom phenol + def2-SVPD. REPRODUCIBLE/CONVERGED active-space variant (PARALLEL).
#
# Problem (diagnosed 2026-06-30): same input gave 532.6 vs 523.9 nm (0.04 eV). Ground
# state + bare EOM-CCSD are bit-identical; the split is in the STEOM active-space build.
# A high-double-excitation-character EA-EOM state near the active boundary is "faked"/
# excluded inconsistently, and which root the parallel Davidson catches is FP-order
# dependent -> the STEOM dressing (hence the excitation) shifts ~0.04 eV run-to-run.
#
# Fix (per ORCA 6.1 STEOM manual -- NOT by tightening OThresh/VThresh, which the manual
# warns against: a bigger active space pulls in MORE doubles-polluted states):
#   DoDbFilter true   -> deterministically excludes IP/EA states with insufficient
#                        singles character (fixed IPThresh/EAThresh), instead of the
#                        ad-hoc parallel-order-dependent faking. => reproducible.
#   NRootsCISNAT 10    -> was 0 (warned "lower than NRoots 5"); set >NRoots for a robust
#                        state-averaged-NTO active-space determination.
#   OThresh/VThresh    -> left at the recommended default 1e-3 (do NOT go below).
# Stays parallel (8 ranks). Final STEOM states should now be >98% active (converged).
%maxcore 4000
%pal nprocs 8 end
%pointcharges "field.pc"
%mdci
  NRoots 5
  DoRootWise true
  FollowCIS true
  RootHoming true
  CheckEachRoot true
  DTol 1e-5
  DoStoreSTEOM true
  AddL2Term True
  DoDbFilter true
  NRootsCISNAT 10
  TCutPNOSingles 1e-12
  NDav 400
  MaxIter 400
  DoSTEOMNatTransOrb true
end
* xyzfile -1 1 geom_cthrp.xyz
